Analyze this {language} code for cryptographic weaknesses (OWASP A02).

Source file:
{source}

Already reported by mechanical pattern analysis — do NOT report these again:
{known_findings}

Detect:
- Broken or deprecated algorithms (MD5, SHA-1, DES, 3DES, RC4, ECB mode)
- Passwords stored with a plain hash instead of bcrypt, scrypt or Argon2
- Predictable randomness used for tokens, session ids, salts or keys
- Hardcoded, reused or derived-from-constant encryption keys and IVs
- Missing or disabled TLS certificate validation
- Secrets compared with a non-constant-time equality check
- Encryption without integrity (no authenticated mode, no MAC)
- Key material logged, serialized or committed alongside the ciphertext

Return a JSON array of findings. Each finding:
{{
  "weakness_type": "WEAK_ALGORITHM|WEAK_PASSWORD_HASH|WEAK_RANDOM|HARDCODED_KEY|TLS_DISABLED|TIMING_UNSAFE|NO_INTEGRITY|KEY_EXPOSURE|OTHER",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "description": "one sentence describing the specific weakness",
  "fix": "concrete fix suggestion"
}}

Return [] if no issues found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
